# =============================================================================
# DENY-BY-DEFAULT — this is a HOME DIRECTORY, not a project repo.
# =============================================================================
# C:\Users\Garrett was initialised as a git repo with 0 commits and no ignore
# file. Without this file, a single `git add .` — run by a human, an agent, or
# an unattended overnight job — would stage credentials and sealed legal
# material, including:
#
#   Downloads/client_secret_*.apps.googleusercontent.com.json   (live OAuth secret)
#   AppData/Local/hermes/.env, auth.json                        (API credentials)
#   .claude.json, .mcp-auth/, .gitconfig, .docker/              (tokens/config)
#   Turner_Case_*/, Landry_CasinoTech_Matter_*/                 (legal PII)
#   Baxley_DoNotProduce_Index_*.md, HCC_Coleman_Appeal_Brief.md (do-not-produce)
#   ~46 nested project repos
#
# Ignoring everything makes that accident impossible. Nothing is currently
# tracked, so this costs nothing.
#
# Project repos (Sports, Sports-canonical-*, Clouds-bruh, ...) each have their
# own .git and are UNAFFECTED — this file has no bearing on them.
#
# To intentionally track something here later, add an explicit negation below,
# e.g.:   !.bashrc
# Never replace this file with a permissive one. Add narrow exceptions instead.
# =============================================================================

*

# The ignore file itself stays committable, so this protection can be recorded.
!.gitignore
